{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/h7mjy1","slide":3,"text":"[Timing: 4 minutes]\nExplain Precision vs Found Rate: Precision@5 is lower because we retrieve 5 chunks and usually only one exact expected recommendation is counted. Found Rate@5 is the key RAG metric because it confirms the right evidence reaches the generator.\nSay why k=5: it reached 100% found rate on the current test set, while k=1 missed many.\n[Sources]\nevaluate.py, data/evaluation/evaluation_summary.json, data/evaluation/evaluation_summary_k1/k3/k4.json."}
